# Normalize line endings so a Windows lane cannot silently commit CRLF.
#
# This is not cosmetic. A CRLF flip in `crates/dig-node-core/src/lib.rs` disabled
# the §908 blind-serve custody guard: it splits on "\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {",
# a needle with an INTERIOR newline, which cannot match under CRLF. The .expect()
# panicked, the guard scanned nothing, and the only signal was one failing test.
#
# A needle with only a LEADING newline still matches CRLF, which is why the
# neighbouring dig-wallet guard survived the same flip -- so the failure is
# selective and reads as unrelated.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and fixture files that must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.wasm binary
*.dig binary
*.der binary
*.crx binary
